{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Who gives songs in the night</b> — Some say: it speaks of the Place, as in <i>“to declare in the morning and the evening”</i>, and as in <i>“When I see Your heavens, the work of Your fingers, the moon and stars.”</i> And most of the commentators said: the word לא (not) serves itself alone and another with it, and so it is: <i>“and he did not say, ‘Where is El my Maker?’—he did not give songs in the night.”</i>"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads the לא of the verse as applying both to what precedes and what follows; the second clause therefore also takes לא implicitly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:35.250254040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}